Note: ============================================================
Note:  Chapter: SFZ Orchestral Sampler (Phase 33)
Note:  Run: dotnet run --project flow-interpreter examples/symphony/sfz_smoke.flow
Note: ============================================================
Note:
Note:  Phase 33 ships a real SFZ-format orchestral sampler — gated behind
Note:  `use "@sfz"` — so composers can load CC-licensed external libraries
Note:  (blessed: VSCO Community CE 1.1.0) via `loadSfz #violin` style calls.
Note:
Note:  This tutorial chapter renders a 4-bar single-violin melody through
Note:  the @sfz surface. Setup instructions:
Note:    1. Download VSCO-CE 1.1.0:
Note:         https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE/releases/tag/1.1.0
Note:    2. Extract to `~/.flow/samples/VSCO-CE/` (or any directory).
Note:    3. Set `sfz_root` in `~/.config/flow/config.toml`:
Note:         sfz_root = "/home/<you>/.flow/samples/VSCO-CE"
Note:    4. Run this script.
Note:
Note:  See examples/symphony/README.md for the full walkthrough.

use "@audio"
use "@sfz"

(print "")
(print "=== SFZ Orchestral Sampler ===")
(print "Loading the violin patch from the configured sfz_root...")

Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: 1. Load the patch via the 19-entry GM symbol dict
Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: `(loadSfz #violin)` resolves `#violin` against the dict shipped in
Note: flow-lang/sfz.flow, joins it with `sfz_root` from your flow config,
Note: and parses the resulting .sfz file. The result is a first-class
Note: `Sfz` value. The `sampler:NAME` instrument string in the renderSong
Note: call below picks the bound patch by variable name.

Sfz violin = (loadSfz #violin)
(print "Violin patch loaded.")

Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: 2. Compose a 4-bar opening melody under tempo + key context
Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: A simple ascending phrase — no articulation marks; the Phase 28
Note: locked envelope rules apply automatically (Normal articulation).

tempo 100 {
    timesig 4/4 {
        key Cmajor {
            section opening {
                Sequence main = | C4q D4q E4q F4q G4h G4h C5w |
            }

Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: 3. Render through the sampler:NAME dispatch
Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: `renderSong song "sampler:violin"` looks up the bound `violin`
Note: patch in the SfzPatchRegistry (Phase 33 D-12) and dispatches to
Note: SfzRenderer for every note. The rendered AudioBuffer rolls through
Note: the same Phase 28 voice-pool + per-section reverb pipeline as the
Note: bundled-sample path — no special handling required.

            Song song = [opening]
            Buffer mix = (renderSong song "sampler:violin")

Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
Note: 4. Export to WAV
Note: -----------------------------------------------------------
            (writeWav "sfz_smoke.wav" mix)
            (print "Wrote sfz_smoke.wav. Play with: aplay sfz_smoke.wav")
        }
    }
}
